 "text": "One word makes people say yes, and it's not please. In 1978, psychologist Ellen Langer tested it at a busy copy machine. Strangers asked to cut in line, three different ways. First, I have five pages, may I use the copy machine? 60% said yes. Second, because I'm in a rush? 94% said yes. Third, because I have to make copies? Of course you do. It's a copy machine. Still, 93% said yes. Here's the trick. Your brain runs on autopilot. It hears because and assumes a good reason is coming, so it stops checking. But there's a catch. For 20 pages, the empty because did nothing. Small favor? Say because. Big favor? Bring a real reason. Follow for more mind tricks.",
